<html>

<head>
    <style>
        @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
            body {
                background: #333;
                color: white;
            }
            a {
                color: skyblue;
            }
        }
        .container {
            font-family: sans-serif;
            max-width: 800px;
            margin: 0 auto;
        }
        .intro {
            text-align: center;
        }
        .licenses-list {
            list-style-type: none;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
        }
        .license-used-by {
            margin-top: -10px;
        }
        .license-text {
            max-height: 200px;
            overflow-y: scroll;
            white-space: pre-wrap;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>
    <main class="container">
        <div class="intro">
            <h1>Kupferdraht — Third-Party Licenses</h1>
            <p>
                This page lists every crate Kupferdraht links against, grouped by the
                license it is distributed under. Regenerated via
                <code>cargo about generate about.hbs &gt; docs/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.html</code>.
            </p>
        </div>
    
        <h2>Overview of licenses:</h2>
        <ul class="licenses-overview">
            {{#each overview}}
            <li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}})</li>
            {{/each}}
        </ul>

        <h2>Components outside the crate graph:</h2>
        <p>
            cargo-about lists the crates of the Cargo graph. Two components
            Kupferdraht ships are not in that list and are recorded here by
            hand; keep this block in step with <code>vendor/README.md</code>
            and <code>kupferdraht-core/Cargo.toml</code>.
        </p>
        <ul class="licenses-list">
            <li class="license">
                <h3>SQLite3 Multiple Ciphers 2.5.1 (SQLite 3.53.4)</h3>
                <p>
                    The whole-database encryption engine under every Kupferdraht
                    database, vendored as the amalgamation in
                    <code>vendor/sqlite3mc/</code> and compiled by the
                    <code>libsqlite3-sys</code> stand-in in
                    <code>vendor/libsqlite3-sys/</code> (the MIT-licensed upstream
                    crate, reduced to its bundled path). SQLite3 Multiple Ciphers:
                    MIT License, Copyright (c) 2019-2026 Ulrich Telle,
                    <code>vendor/sqlite3mc/LICENSE</code>; provenance and checksums in
                    <code>vendor/sqlite3mc/PROVENANCE.txt</code>. SQLite itself is in
                    the public domain.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li class="license">
                <h3>sqlite-remote-vfs 0.5.0 and sqlite-remote-protocol 0.5.0</h3>
                <p>
                    The browser target's storage VFS (ADR-0035), a git dependency of
                    <code>kupferdraht-core</code> pinned by revision. The crates are
                    marked <code>publish = false</code>, so cargo-about treats them as
                    private and leaves them out. Apache License 2.0, Schwarz Digits,
                    <a href="https://github.com/SchwarzDigits/sqlite-remote-vfs">github.com/SchwarzDigits/sqlite-remote-vfs</a>.
                </p>
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>All license text:</h2>
        <ul class="licenses-list">
            {{#each licenses}}
            <li class="license">
                <h3 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h3>
                <h4>Used by:</h4>
                <ul class="license-used-by">
                    {{#each used_by}}
                    <li><a href="{{#if crate.repository}} {{crate.repository}} {{else}} https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}} {{/if}}">{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</a></li>
                    {{/each}}
                </ul>
                <pre class="license-text">{{text}}</pre>
            </li>
            {{/each}}
        </ul>
    </main>
</body>

</html>
